{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789779154,"nonce":"JxKUTIov7fanhyPXr0RNN69zK/Y=","title":"LLVM execution engine dropped after its context: fault at exit","message":"The interpreter's tick callbacks capture the tier backends (the LLVM one\nthrough an Arc), and TieredRuntime drops its backend, which owns the LLVM\ncontext, before its interpreter. The last Arc then dropped the MCJIT\nengine against a freed context: EXC_BAD_ACCESS in\nLLVMContext::removeModule from TieredRuntime's drop glue, after the\nprogram had printed its answer (nqueens, every run under ZYPY_LLVM=1).\n\nFix: the runtime's shutdown clears the interpreter's bridge and tick\ncallbacks before shutting the backend down.","files":null}]}